		category: 'Fauna',
		content:
			'<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">references</div>\r\n          <h4>References:</h4>\r\n          <LanguageSets>\r\n            <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>צְפַרְדֵּעַ</em> \r\n            [tsefarde‘a] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="EXO 7:27_{00030}" title="EXO 7:27_{00030}">00200702700030</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="EXO 7:28_{00010}" title="EXO 7:28_{00010}">00200702800010</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="EXO 7:29_{00024}" title="EXO 7:29_{00024}">00200702900024</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="EXO 8:1_{00056}" title="EXO 8:1_{00056}">00200800100056</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="EXO 8:2_{00024}" title="EXO 8:2_{00024}">00200800200024</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="EXO 8:3_{00024}" title="EXO 8:3_{00024}">00200800300024</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="EXO 8:4_{00034}" title="EXO 8:4_{00034}">00200800400034</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="EXO 8:5_{00042}" title="EXO 8:5_{00042}">00200800500042</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="EXO 8:7_{00008}" title="EXO 8:7_{00008}">00200800700008</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="EXO 8:8_{00034}" title="EXO 8:8_{00034}">00200800800034</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="EXO 8:9_{00020}" title="EXO 8:9_{00020}">00200800900020</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="PSA 78:45_{00014}" title="PSA 78:45_{00014}">01907804500014</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="PSA 105:30_{00006}" title="PSA 105:30_{00006}">01910503000006</span>\r\n            </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>βάτραχος</em> \r\n            [batrachos] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="REV 16:13_{00048}" title="REV 16:13_{00048}">06601601300048</span>\r\n              <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="WIS 19:10_{00050}" title="WIS 19:10_{00050}">07001901000050</span>\r\n            </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </LanguageSets>\r\n          <Paragraphs />\r\n        </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">discussion</div>\r\n          <h4>Discussion:</h4>\r\n          <SubHeading />\r\n          <LanguageSets />\r\n          <Paragraphs>\r\n            <p><div class="image-box">Image: WEB-0247_frog</div>There is little doubt that the Hebrew and Greek words mean “frog". The plague of frogs mentioned in Exodus comes after the plague of polluted water. The frogs seem to have left the water and come into the villages. Since frogs eat flies and thus control fly populations, it seems likely that the death of the frogs was one of the causes of the next two plagues to trouble Egypt, namely gnats and flies.</p>\r\n          </Paragraphs>\r\n        </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">description</div>\r\n          <h4>Description:</h4>\r\n          <SubHeading />\r\n          <LanguageSets />\r\n          <Paragraphs>\r\n            <p><div class="image-box">Image: WEB-0248_frogs</div>The two most common frogs in the Middle East and Egypt are the Edible Frog <i>Rana esculenta</i> and the Spotted Frog <i>Rana punctata</i>. They are both about 70 millimeters (3 inches) long and are brown or olive-green in color. They live in the water almost all of the time and eat gnats, flies, and other waterside insects. They lay eggs, which hatch as tadpoles and gradually grow legs. The hind legs are much bigger and better developed than the front legs, since the hind legs are used for jumping.</p>\r\n          </Paragraphs>\r\n        </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">special significance or symbolism</div>\r\n          <h4>Special significance or symbolism:</h4>\r\n          <SubHeading />\r\n          <LanguageSets />\r\n          <Paragraphs>\r\n            <p>Frogs were considered unclean by the Jews and also by the Egyptians and Persians, who associated them with demons.</p>\r\n          </Paragraphs>\r\n        </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">translation</div>\r\n          <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n          <SubHeading />\r\n          <LanguageSets />\r\n          <Paragraphs>\r\n            <p>Frogs are found all over the world, and there should be no problem in finding a local equivalent.</p>\r\n          </Paragraphs>\r\n              <BibleImages>\r\n                <BibleImage Type="ILL" Id="WEB-0247_frog">\r\n                  <Collection>WEB</Collection>\r\n                  <Path>marble-images-flora-fauna-realia\\FAUNA</Path>\r\n                  <FileName>WEB-0247_frog.jpg</FileName>\r\n                  <Copyright>Pixabay</Copyright>\r\n                  <Definition Id=""  LanguageCode="en"></Definition>\r\n                  <Caption>Frog</Caption>\r\n                  <Description />\r\n                </BibleImage>\r\n                <BibleImage Type="ILL" Id="WEB-0248_frogs">\r\n                  <Collection>WEB</Collection>\r\n                  <Path>marble-images-flora-fauna-realia\\FAUNA</Path>\r\n                  <FileName>WEB-0248_frogs.jpg</FileName>\r\n                  <Copyright>Pixabay</Copyright>\r\n                  <Definition Id=""  LanguageCode="en"></Definition>\r\n                  <Caption>Frogs</Caption>\r\n                  <Description />\r\n                </BibleImage>\r\n              </BibleImages>\r\n        </div>',
