				html: '\r\n          <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n          <SubHeading />\r\n          <LanguageSets />\r\n          <Paragraphs>\r\n            <p>What we see in the various English versions of <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="ISA 44:14_{00014}" title="ISA 44:14_{00014}">02304401400014</span> for the translation of <i>tirzah</i> (for example, “holm,” “plane,” “fir,” “oak,” and “cypress”) are only guesses. A reasonable solution then, is to follow the suggestion of Zohary, which at least has some basis in paleobiology and linguistics, and use a transliteration from a major language (for example, <i>pino</i>, <i>payin</i>, and <i>pinyola</i>). In a receptor culture-oriented translation translators could substitute an appropriate tree whose wood is commonly used for carving images, as long as the name is not being used in the translation for some other tree.</p>\r\n            <p>“Pine nuts” from China are now being sold in the United States as a salad ingredient. We assume these to be from a sub-species of the stone pine.</p>\r\n          </Paragraphs>\r\n              <BibleImages>\r\n                <BibleImage Type="ILL" Id="WEB-0719_pine_stone">\r\n                  <Collection>WEB</Collection>\r\n                  <Path>marble-images-flora-fauna-realia\\FAUNA</Path>\r\n                  <FileName>WEB-0719_pine_stone.jpg</FileName>\r\n                  <Copyright>Serge Melki (Wikimedia Commons)</Copyright>\r\n                  <Definition Id="" LanguageCode="en"></Definition>\r\n                  <Caption>Stone pine</Caption>\r\n                  <Description />\r\n                </BibleImage>\r\n                <BibleImage Type="ILL" Id="WEB-0718_pine_cone">\r\n                  <Collection>WEB</Collection>\r\n                  <Path>marble-images-flora-fauna-realia\\FAUNA</Path>\r\n                  <FileName>WEB-0718_pine_cone.jpg</FileName>\r\n                  <Copyright>Luis Fernández García (Wikimedia Commons)</Copyright>\r\n                  <Definition Id="" LanguageCode="en"></Definition>\r\n                  <Caption>Stone pine (cone)</Caption>\r\n                  <Description />\r\n                </BibleImage>\r\n              </BibleImages>\r\n        '
