				html: '\r\n          <h4>Description:</h4>\r\n          <SubHeading />\r\n          <LanguageSets />\r\n          <Paragraphs>\r\n            <p><div class="image-box">Image: WEB-0852_sycomore_fig</div>The sycomore fig is not a tall tree (up to 10 meters [33 feet]) but has large low, spreading branches—just right for a short man to climb up in order to see over a crowd of taller people (see the story of Zacchaeus in <span class="ref-link" data-usfm="LUK 19:4_{00016}" title="LUK 19:4_{00016}">04201900400016</span>). The fruit, while edible, is not as juicy or sweet as the more common variety. The most unusual thing about the fruit is that it grows in bunches right on the trunk and branches of the tree rather than among the leaves.</p>\r\n          </Paragraphs>\r\n        '
