		content:
			'<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">references</div>\r\n        <h4>References:</h4>\r\n        <LanguageSets>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>מֶתֶג</em> \r\n            [metheg] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H01201902800030</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01903200900020</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02002600300010</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02303702900030</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>רֶסֶן</em> \r\n            [resen] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H01804100500014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01903200900024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02303002800032</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>χαλινός</em> \r\n            [chalinos] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>G05900300300012</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G06601402000032</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>χρυσοχάλινος</em> \r\n            [chrusochalinos] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>L07801002900024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>L08100300600028</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>κόσμος</em> \r\n            [kosmos] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>L07800500300044</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>σαγή</em> \r\n            [sagē] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>L07800302500024</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </LanguageSets>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">description</div>\r\n        <h4>Description:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <image id="UBS-0009_bronze_horse_bit.jpg" />The bit was a short bar, usually made of metal, placed in the mouth of a horse. Its ends, which projected from the mouth of the animal, were attached to ropes or leather straps that fitted over the head as the bridle.</p>\r\n          <p>———</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">usage</div>\r\n        <h4>Usage:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <image id="WEB-0969_harness_bridle_en.jpg" />By pulling on the bridle straps to the right or left, the rider or driver of the wagon could control the actions of the horse.</p>\r\n          <p>———</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">translation</div>\r\n        <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <image id="WEB-0932_horse.jpg" />The Hebrew words <i>metheg</i> and <i>resen</i> respectively refer to the “bit” and “bridle” (although <a>RSV</a> has once rendered <i>metheg</i> as “bridle” in <s>H02002600300010</s>). The Greek words <i>chalinos</i> and <i>chrusochalinos</i> refer to both the bit and bridle. Where a bit or bridle as a piece of harness is unknown, translators can use a descriptive phrase, such as “something to guide a horse with” or “something to put in the mouth of a horse to guide it.”</p>\r\n          <p>The Hebrew word <i>mtsilah</i> in <s>H03801402000016</s> probably refers to some sort of noise-making decoration on the harness of a horse. The word occurs only here in the Bible.</p>\r\n          <p>In <s>G06601402000032</s> the reference to “a horse’s bridle” (<a>RSV</a>) is merely an indication of measurement. It refers to the height of the bridle from the ground, so we may render this measurement as “about a meter and a half” (<a>FRCL</a>) or “about five feet” (<a>GNT</a>).</p>\r\n          <p>The Greek word used in <s>L07801002900024</s> and <s>L08100300600028</s> indicates that the metal parts of the bridle were made of gold.</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n        <BibleImages>\r\n          <BibleImage id="UBS-0009_bronze_horse_bit">\r\n            <FileName>UBS-0009_bronze_horse_bit.jpg</FileName>\r\n            <Collection>UBS</Collection>\r\n            <Copyright>© Deutsche Bibelgesellschaft, Stuttgart by United Bible Societies</Copyright>\r\n            <Caption>Ancient bronze horse bit</Caption>\r\n          </BibleImage>\r\n          <BibleImage id="WEB-0969_harness_bridle_en">\r\n            <FileName>WEB-0969_harness_bridle_en.jpg</FileName>\r\n            <Collection>WEB</Collection>\r\n            <Copyright>© Gary Todd - Wikimedia Commons</Copyright>\r\n            <Caption>Harness with bridle and bit fitted on the horse\'s head</Caption>\r\n          </BibleImage>\r\n          <BibleImage id="WEB-0932_horse">\r\n            <FileName>WEB-0932_horse.jpg</FileName>\r\n            <Collection>WEB</Collection>\r\n            <Copyright>© Wikimedia Commons</Copyright>\r\n            <Caption>Horse and rider showing use of reins</Caption>\r\n          </BibleImage>\r\n        </BibleImages>\r\n      </div>',
