				html: '\r\n        <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>Translators and commentators differ concerning the exact meaning of the Hebrew word <i>m’adam</i>. Most understand it to mean that the rams’ skins or sheep­skins (which it always modifies) have been “dyed red” (<a>GNT</a>, <a>NIV</a>, <a>NJB</a>) or “colored red” (<a>FRCL</a>, <a>PV</a>). However, <a>RSV</a>, <a>CEV</a>, and <a>REB</a> say “tanned” (see <l>1.13 Leather&lt;REALIA:1.13&gt;</l>).</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      '
