				html: '\r\n        <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <s>H02304401300024</s>: This verse mentions three tools used by a carpenter in making an idol from a piece of wood. All three tools are mentioned only here in the Bible, and their meanings are derived primarily from the context and from their etymologies. Two of the tools, the <i>sered</i> (see <l>1.12.6 Stylus, marker&lt;REALIA:1.12.6&gt;</l>) and the <i>mchugah</i> (see <l>1.12.7 Compass, circle instrument&lt;REALIA:1.12.7&gt;</l>), have to do with marking the wood before carving it, while the <i>maqtsu‘a</i> was used to cut and shape the wood into the desired form.</p>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <a>GNT</a> combines <i>maqtsu‘a</i> and <i>mchugah</i> in the generic rendering “tools.” This may serve for cultures where the chisel or plane is not known. It is also possible to render <i>maqtsu‘a</i> as “knife.”</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n        <BibleImages>\r\n          <BibleImage id="OAI-0021_woodcrafting_chisel">\r\n            <FileName>OAI-0021_woodcrafting_chisel.png</FileName>\r\n            <Collection>OPEN-AI</Collection>\r\n            <Copyright>Image generated by ChatGPT using OpenAI technology</Copyright>\r\n            <Caption>Man crafting a piece of wood with a chisel</Caption>\r\n          </BibleImage>\r\n        </BibleImages>\r\n      '
