		category: 'Realia',
		content:
			'<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">references</div>\r\n        <h4>References:</h4>\r\n        <LanguageSets>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>קַרְקַע</em> \r\n            [qarqa‘] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H00400501700034</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100601600034</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100603000006</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100700700038</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100700700044</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </LanguageSets>\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>———</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">translation</div>\r\n        <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>The Hebrew word <i>qarqa‘</i> in <s>H00400501700034</s> describes the unpaved dirt floor of the Tabernacle. We are not told if Solomon’s Temple had paved floors, but since <s>H01100603000006</s> says that he overlaid them with gold, we may assume that they had some kind of paving, either wood or stone.</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      </div>',
