			'<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">references</div>\r\n        <h4>References:</h4>\r\n        <LanguageSets>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>כֹּתֶל</em> \r\n            [kothel] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H02200200900028</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Aramaic</strong>\r\n            <em>כְּתַל</em> \r\n            [kethal] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>A01500500800046</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>A02700500500034</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>קִיר</em> \r\n            [qir] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H00301403700022</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00301403700046</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00301403900036</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00901801100030</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00901901000028</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00901901000054</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00902002500028</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00902502200042</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00902503400064</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01000501100036</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100501300042</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100600600080</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100601500008</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100601500034</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100602700050</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100602700070</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100602900008</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01101401000028</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01101601100038</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01102102100030</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01200401000008</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01200900800024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01200903300026</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01202000200014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01301400100030</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </LanguageSets>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">description</div>\r\n        <h4>Description:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <image id="WEB-0409_wall.jpg" />A wall is the verticle surface that forms one side of a building or room. It supports the ceiling of a room or the roof of a building. We distinguish here between this kind of wall in a building and a city wall (see <l>3.13.3.1 City wall, rampart, battlement&lt;REALIA:3.13.3.1&gt;</l>) or a boundary wall (see <l>3.6 Boundary wall, fence&lt;REALIA:3.6&gt;</l>).</p>\r\n          <p>———</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">translation</div>\r\n        <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>The Hebrew word <i>qir</i> can refer to both the outer wall and the inner wall of a structure. Where a language has distinct words for these different walls, the translator will need to pay close attention to the context. For example, <s>H01100501300042</s> mentions “the hyssop that grows out of the wall” (<a>RSV</a>). This “wall” is more likely an external wall rather than one inside a house.</p>\r\n          <p>In <s>H00902502200042 H00902503400064 H01101401000028 H01101601100038 H01102102100030</s>; and<s>H01200900800024</s> there is a Hebrew phrase that is literally “one who urinates against a wall.” This phrase refers to men, so most translations say “man/men” or “male[s].”</p>\r\n          <p>In <s>H01000501100036</s> and <s>H01301400100030</s><a>RSV</a> says that King Hiram of Tyre sent Solomon “masons,” which is literally “wall-stone workers/cutters” in Hebrew. These were men who shaped stones so they fit together neatly in a wall. <a>GNT</a> says “stone masons,” and <a>CEV</a> has “stone workers.”</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n        <BibleImages>\r\n          <BibleImage id="WEB-0409_wall">\r\n            <FileName>WEB-0409_wall.jpg</FileName>\r\n            <Collection>WEB</Collection>\r\n            <Copyright>MM, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons</Copyright>\r\n            <Caption>Fitted stones in a wall</Caption>\r\n          </BibleImage>\r\n        </BibleImages>\r\n      </div>',
