		category: 'Realia',
		content:
			'<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">references</div>\r\n        <h4>References:</h4>\r\n        <LanguageSets>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>בַּיִת, אָסֹף</em> \r\n            [(beyth) ’asupim] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H01601202500024</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>אוֹצָר</em> \r\n            [’otsar] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H01302702700030</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01302702800034</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01401101100022</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01601204400028</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01601301200032</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01601301300008</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01803802200008</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01803802200014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01903300700020</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01913500700030</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02303900200078</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02303900400046</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02401001300054</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02403801100034</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02405101600048</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>ἀποδοχεῖον</em> \r\n            [apodocheion] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>L07100101700018</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>θησαυρός</em> \r\n            [thēsauros] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>L07104101200022</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>L07104301400008</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>ταμεῖον</em> \r\n            [tameion] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>G04201202400024</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </LanguageSets>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">description</div>\r\n        <h4>Description:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>The places listed above were for general storage. Their shape and structure are undefined. See also <l>3.13.4 Armory, arsenal&lt;REALIA:3.13.4&gt;</l> and <l>3.14.1.4 Treasury, strongroom&lt;REALIA:3.14.1.4&gt;</l>.</p>\r\n          <p>———</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">translation</div>\r\n        <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>In most of the references listed above it is stated what was being stored. Where the commodity being stored is named, languages may have a special word for the particular place where such a commodity is stored; for example, in <s>H01302702700030</s><a>GNT</a> has “Wine cellars” for the Hebrew word <i>’otsar</i>. However, in the following verse, where the same word is used together with “oil,” <a>GNT</a> has “Olive oil storage,” because English has no special word for a place to store olive oil.</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      </div>',
