				html: '\r\n        <h4>Description:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>The Holy Place was the interior of the Jerusalem Temple or of the earlier Tabernacle. This interior contained two rooms, an outer one and an inner one. “Holy Place” may refer to either one of these rooms. Most often “Holy Place” refers to the larger room outside the veil, while the smaller room on its west end is called the “Most Holy Place” or “Holy of Holies” (see <l>3.15.2.2 Holy of Holies, Most Holy Place&lt;REALIA:3.15.2.2&gt;</l>). In the Tabernacle the Holy Place measured 10 by 20 cubits (5 by 10 meters; 16.5 by 33 feet), while in the Temple it was 20 cubits by 40 cubits (10 by 20 meters; 33 by 66 feet).</p>\r\n          <p>———</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      '
