		content:
			'<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">references</div>\r\n        <h4>References:</h4>\r\n        <LanguageSets>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>ἀποσυνάγωγος</em> \r\n            [aposunagōgos] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>G04300902200042</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04301204200038</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04301600200002</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>ἀρχισυνάγωγος</em> \r\n            [archisunagōgos] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>G04100502200010</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04100503600020</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04100503800014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04200804900016</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04201301400008</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401301500024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401800800008</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401801700012</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>συναγωγή</em> \r\n            [sunagōgē] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>G04000402300020</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04000600200030</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04000600500026</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04000903500028</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04001001700028</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04001200900014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04001305400022</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04002300600026</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04002303400048</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04100102100024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04100102300012</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04100102900010</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04100103900012</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04100300100012</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04100600200016</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04101203900010</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04101300900022</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04200401500012</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04200401600042</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04200402000030</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04200402800014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04200403300008</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04200403800010</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04200404400012</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04200600600020</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04200700500016</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04200804100024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04201104300022</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04201201100014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04201301000014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04202004600040</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04202101200032</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04300605900008</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04301802000026</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04400600900014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04400900200018</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04400902000010</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401300500024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401301400032</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401304300008</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401400100024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401502100028</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401700100026</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401701000040</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401701700012</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401800400010</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401800700040</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401801900026</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401802600014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04401900800010</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04402201900028</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04402401200036</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G04402601100010</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G05900200200010</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G06600200900048</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>G06600300900010</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </LanguageSets>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">description and usage</div>\r\n        <h4>Description and usage:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <image id="PTZ-0077_synagogue_nazareth_outside.jpg" />\r\n          </p>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <image id="PTZ-0076_synagogue_nazareth_inside.jpg" /> The synagogue was a building for assemblies, associated with religious activity (normally a building in which Jewish worship took place and in which the Law was taught). Synagogues were not normally large structures in New Testament times, and often they were not much larger than a home.</p>\r\n          <p>———</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">translation</div>\r\n        <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>Synagogues are mentioned frequently in the New Testament, but surprisingly little is known about their physical structure at that time, since almost none have been excavated which can be dated definitely to the time of Jesus. While they probably had a literal “orientation” (that is, facing east), they had little of a distinctive architecture until after the period of the New Testament. Fortunately, it is not essential for the task of the translator to know details of the structure of the synagogue.</p>\r\n          <p>It is important to distinguish clearly between “synagogue” and “temple,” and it is not enough to speak of synagogues merely as “small temples.” There were many synagogues, but only one Temple in Jerusalem, the only place for Jewish sacrifices. It is better either to borrow a term for synagogue or to employ a descriptive equivalent such as “place where Jewish people worshiped God” or “building for worshiping God.”</p>\r\n          <p>It is also important to distinguish in translation between “synagogue” and “church,” whether these terms refer to the congregation or to the building.</p>\r\n          <p>The Greek word <i>sunagōgē</i> appears about a dozen times in the Deuterocanon, always with the meaning of a congregation or assembly of people. It should never be rendered in these books as some kind of building.</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n        <BibleImages>\r\n          <BibleImage id="PTZ-0077_synagogue_nazareth_outside">\r\n            <FileName>PTZ-0077_synagogue_nazareth_outside.jpg</FileName>\r\n            <Collection>PRITZ</Collection>\r\n            <Copyright>© Ray Pritz by United Bible Societies</Copyright>\r\n            <Caption>A reconstruction of the synagogue at Nazareth</Caption>\r\n          </BibleImage>\r\n          <BibleImage id="PTZ-0076_synagogue_nazareth_inside">\r\n            <FileName>PTZ-0076_synagogue_nazareth_inside.jpg</FileName>\r\n            <Collection>PRITZ</Collection>\r\n            <Copyright>© Ray Pritz by United Bible Societies</Copyright>\r\n            <Caption>A reconstruction of the interior of the synagogue at Nazareth</Caption>\r\n          </BibleImage>\r\n        </BibleImages>\r\n      </div>',
