		content:
			'<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">references</div>\r\n        <h4>References:</h4>\r\n        <LanguageSets>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>יָע</em> \r\n            [ya‘] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H00202700300014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00203800300028</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00400401400040</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100704000020</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01100704500016</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01202501400016</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01400401100020</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01400401600016</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02405201800016</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </LanguageSets>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">description and usage</div>\r\n        <h4>Description and usage:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <image id="WEB-0455_shovel.jpg" />The scraper was used to remove the refuse from the altar after a victim had been burned. It may have resembled a kind of shovel, with which the ashes could be lifted, or a kind of rake or hoe, with which they could be scraped into the bronze pot (see <l>4.4.1 Pan, pot, pail&lt;REALIA:4.4.1&gt;</l>).</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n        <BibleImages>\r\n          <BibleImage id="WEB-0455_shovel">\r\n            <FileName>WEB-0455_shovel.jpg</FileName>\r\n            <Collection>WEB</Collection>\r\n            <Copyright>Gary Todd, Israel Museum, CC0, via Wikimedia Commons</Copyright>\r\n            <Caption>Large shovels to remove refuse from the altar</Caption>\r\n          </BibleImage>\r\n        </BibleImages>\r\n      </div>',
