				html: '\r\n        <h4>Description and usage:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <image id="WEB-0457_libation.jpg" />The libation in the Tabernacle and Temple was the pouring out of wine as an offering to God. Two vessels were involved in this operation. From the first vessel the wine was poured into the second one. Both vessels were placed on the table for consecrated bread (see <l>4.3.5 Table for consecrated bread&lt;REALIA:4.3.5&gt;</l>) and are only mentioned in connection with that table. The first container was a kind of jar or pitcher (<i>qaswah</i> in Hebrew), and the second one was a small bowl (<i>mnaqith</i> in Hebrew). Both objects were made of gold.</p>\r\n          <p>———</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      '
