			'<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">references</div>\r\n        <h4>References:</h4>\r\n        <LanguageSets>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>כָּנָף</em> \r\n            [kanaf] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H00401503800026</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00401503800044</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00502201200012</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00502300100020</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00502702000016</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00800300900024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00901502700018</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00902400600028</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00902401200014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00902401200030</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02400203400006</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02600500300024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02601600800026</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H03700201200014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H03700201200024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H03800802300044</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </LanguageSets>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">description</div>\r\n        <h4>Description:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <image id="OAI-0007_pharisee_en.png" />The hem was the lower edge of an outer garment (see <l>6.2 Outer garment, cloak, mantle, robe&lt;REALIA:6.2&gt;</l>).</p>\r\n          <p>———</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">usage</div>\r\n        <h4>Usage:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>See <l>6.2.1.1 Fringe, tassel&lt;REALIA:6.2.1.1&gt;</l>.</p>\r\n          <p>———</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">translation</div>\r\n        <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>Most translations render the Hebrew word <i>kanaf</i> in <s>H00401503800026</s> and <s>H00502201200012</s> as “corners” (<a>RSV</a>, <a>GNT</a>). In <s>H00401503800026</s><a>CEV</a> says “bottom edge,” which may also serve as a model.</p>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <s>H03800802300044</s>: While the word <i>kanaf</i> indicates the lower edge of a garment, it is sometimes used for the garment itself (compare <s>H02400203400006 H02601600800026</s>). In such passages it may be possible to use a word for the outer garment. Two models for the first part of <s>H03800802300044</s> are “When this happens, ten people from nations with different languages will grab a Jew by his clothes” (<a>CEV</a>) and “At that time, ten men from different countries will come and take hold of a Judean by his coat” (<a>NCV</a>). <a>GNT</a> “In those days ten foreigners will come to one Jew” is also possible, although it loses the element of urgency conveyed by the act of grabbing hold of the robe.</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n        <BibleImages>\r\n          <BibleImage id="OAI-0007_pharisee_en">\r\n            <FileName>OAI-0007_pharisee_en.png</FileName>\r\n            <Collection>OPEN-AI</Collection>\r\n            <Copyright>Image generated by ChatGPT using OpenAI technology</Copyright>\r\n            <Caption>A Pharisee, wearing phylactery and prayer shawl</Caption>\r\n          </BibleImage>\r\n        </BibleImages>\r\n      </div>',
