				type: 'translation',
				html: '\r\n        <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>In many cultures a widow can be identified by her dress or some other external sign. In some places she will wear black or white for a certain period of time or even for the rest of her life. Where such a custom exists, a translation may use the word for the clothing or other symbol that identifies the widow.</p>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <s>H00502401701000</s> mentions the “cloak of a widow.” This does not seem to be a garment peculiar to widows only but a normal cloak worn by everyone (see <l>6.2 Outer garment, cloak, mantle, robe&lt;REALIA:6.2&gt;</l>). Because of the protected status of widows in Israelite society, items of clothing were not to be taken from them. Similarly, in <s>G04400903901000</s> there is no reason to assume that the clothes made by Dorcas were special “widows’ clothing,” although they were certainly women’s clothes.</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      '
