				html: '\r\n        <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>The equivalent of “cymbal” in many languages is a phrase such as “loud metal.”</p>\r\n          <p>In <s>H01915000500006</s> two kinds of cymbals are mentioned, literally “cymbals of hearing” and “cymbals of shouting.” This may mean “small cymbals … large cymbals, or it may be just a poetic variation with the meaning “clanging cymbals … clashing cymbals.”</p>\r\n          <p>In <s>G04601300100036</s><a>GNT</a> renders the Greek word <i>kumbalon</i> as “bell” instead of “cymbal” since it is more widely understood.</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n        <BibleImages>\r\n          <BibleImage id="WEB-0514_cymbals">\r\n            <FileName>WEB-0514_cymbals.jpg</FileName>\r\n            <Collection>WEB</Collection>\r\n            <Copyright>© Finoskov, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons</Copyright>\r\n            <Caption>Cymbals</Caption>\r\n          </BibleImage>\r\n        </BibleImages>\r\n      '
