			'<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">references</div>\r\n        <h4>References:</h4>\r\n        <LanguageSets>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>גַּלְגַּל</em> \r\n            [galgal] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H02602302400014</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02602601000020</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>עֲגָלָה</em> \r\n            [‘agalah] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H00104501900022</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00104502100020</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00104502700030</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00104600500044</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00400700300018</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00400700300030</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00400700600012</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00400700700008</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00400700800010</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00900600700012</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00900600700050</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00900600800022</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00900601000030</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00900601100016</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00900601400006</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00900601400046</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01000600300016</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01000600300056</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01301300700016</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01301300700040</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H01904601000024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02300501800026</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02302802700020</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02302802800024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H03000201300018</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>צָב, עֲגָלָה</em> \r\n            [tsav, ‘egloth tsav] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H00400700300018</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00400700300020</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H02306602000046</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>ἅμαξα</em> \r\n            [hamaxa] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>L06801501100088</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>L07103300500004</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>καρρον</em> \r\n            [karron] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>L08100505300026</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Greek</strong>\r\n            <em>ῥέδη</em> \r\n            [rhedē] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>G06601801300052</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </LanguageSets>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">description and usage</div>\r\n        <h4>Description and usage:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <image id="UBS-0035_wagon_model.jpg" />The wagon was a two or four-wheeled carriage or cart used for travel or the transport of loads. Such vehicles were usually made of wood. They were pulled by draft animals, usually oxen, donkeys, or horses. These animals were attached to a long pole that was in turn attached to the front of the wagon. The upper section of the wagon was often formed by crossed wooden bars in the shape of a cage.</p>\r\n          <p>———</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">translation</div>\r\n        <h4>Translation:</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n        <Paragraphs>\r\n          <p>Wagons and carts in the Bible were always pulled by animals. Translators should avoid any word for “wagon” that indicates a vehicle propelled by an engine.</p>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <image id="OAI-0066_cart_with_yoke_of_oxen.png" />\r\n            <s>H00400700300018</s>: The meaning of the Hebrew phrase <i>‘egloth tsav</i> here is uncertain. Most translators and commentators say something like “covered wagons” (<a>RSV</a>, <a>REB</a>). These would be wagons as described above with a cloth covering the items carried in each wagon. Such a wagon might resemble a tortoise or turtle, which is a meaning of the Hebrew word <i>tsav</i>.</p>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <s>H02602302400014 H02602601000020</s>: The Hebrew word <i>galgal</i> is literally “wheel.” In the context of these verses, it is clear that this is a metonym for a vehicle with wheels, that is, a cart or wagon.</p>\r\n          <p>\r\n            <s>L08100505300026</s>: In this verse some Greek manuscripts have the word <i>chara</i> (“joy”), which makes no sense in this context. One manuscript has the word <i>karron</i>, meaning “wagon” as described above.</p>\r\n        </Paragraphs>\r\n        <BibleImages>\r\n          <BibleImage id="UBS-0035_wagon_model">\r\n            <FileName>UBS-0035_wagon_model.jpg</FileName>\r\n            <Collection>UBS</Collection>\r\n            <Copyright>© Deutsche Bibelgesellschaft, Stuttgart by United Bible Societies</Copyright>\r\n            <Caption>Drawing of a wagon model</Caption>\r\n          </BibleImage>\r\n          <BibleImage id="OAI-0066_cart_with_yoke_of_oxen">\r\n            <FileName>OAI-0066_cart_with_yoke_of_oxen.png</FileName>\r\n            <Collection>OPEN-AI</Collection>\r\n            <Copyright>Image generated by ChatGPT using OpenAI technology</Copyright>\r\n            <Caption>\r\n            </Caption>\r\n          </BibleImage>\r\n        </BibleImages>\r\n      </div>',
