		content:
			'<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">references</div>\r\n        <h4>References:</h4>\r\n        <LanguageSets>\r\n          <div class="lang-set"><strong>Hebrew</strong>\r\n            <em>עֹמֶר</em> \r\n            [‘omer] \r\n            <div class="ref-list">\r\n              <Reference>H00201601600026</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00201601800010</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00201602200026</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00201603200024</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00201603300028</Reference>\r\n              <Reference>H00201603600006</Reference>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </LanguageSets>\r\n        <Paragraphs />\r\n      </div>\n<div class="section-box"><div class="section-label">other</div>\r\n        <h4>In <s>H00201601600026</s> the <i>‘omer</i> was the amount of manna to be gathered. It is expressed by many translations as “two quarts” (<a>GNT</a>). Luther and <a>GECL</a> prefer a container of appropriate size, saying “a jar full.” <s>H00201603600006</s> defines an omer as 1/10 of an ephah.</h4>\r\n        <SubHeading />\r\n        <LanguageSets />\r\n      </div>',
